 to cysteine in a single enzymatic step (C02291 → C00097), establishing cystathionine as a precursor driving cysteine availability for glutathione and selenoprotein synthesis.\n\nThe concurrent elevation of **mercaptopurine** (C02380), a thiopurine analog, is noteworthy. Mercaptopurine is structurally related to the purine salvage pathway and to thiol metabolism, and its co-occurrence with eicosanoid remodeling and sulfur amino acid flux may reflect either oxidative stress imposition or a pharmacologic perturbation targeting overlapping redox-regulated enzymes.\n\n**Biological significance:** The pattern is consistent with a treatment-induced inflammatory or pro-resolving lipid mediator shift — the coordinated 5-LOX products (leukotriene A4, 5-HETE) alongside cytochrome P450 products (15-HETE) and cyclopentenone prostaglandins (15d-PGJ₂) suggests simultaneous activation of multiple arms of the arachidonic acid cascade. The parallel induction of cystathionine → cysteine flux may support heightened demand for reduced glutathione and selenoproteins to counterbalance increased lipid peroxidation load.",
